{"case_id": "CML_BC_TEST_001", "timestep": 3, "case_summary": "A 52-year-old male presents to the emergency department with progressive fatigue,\nnight sweats, abdominal fullness, and blurred vision over the past 3 weeks. Past\nmedical history is unremarkable except for well-controlled hypertension.\n\nPhysical exam reveals:\n- Massive splenomegaly (8 cm below costal margin)\n- Bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots on fundoscopy\n- Scattered petechiae on lower extremities\n\nLaboratory findings:\n- WBC: 145,000/μL with 82% blasts\n- Hemoglobin: 7.2 g/dL\n- Platelets: 28,000/μL\n- Basophilia: 8%\n- LDH: 2,450 U/L (elevated)\n- Uric acid: 11.2 mg/dL (elevated)\n[Answer options redacted — use clinical findings only]", "root": {"label": "Subacute Progressive Constitutional and Hematologic Deficits with Multilineage Cytopenias and Leukemoid Reaction of Uncertain Aetiology", "time_course": "subacute", "severity": "unspecified", "confidence": 0.9, "supporting_facts": ["Progressive fatigue and night sweats over 3 weeks", "Massive splenomegaly (8 cm below costal margin)", "Bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots", "WBC: 145,000/μL with 82% blasts and basophilia", "Severe anemia (Hb: 7.2 g/dL) and thrombocytopenia (Platelets: 28,000/μL)", "Elevated LDH (2450 U/L) and uric acid (11.2 mg/dL)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia (CML): Bcr-Abl testing required for chronic MPN differential, but 82% blasts make blast crisis unlikely", "Acute Infectious Syndrome: Constitutional symptoms are nonspecific; no fever or infectious focus documented", "Hemophagocytic Lymphohistiocytosis (HLH): Not strongly supported by lab features (blasts vs. reactive lymphocytosis)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fatigue, night sweats)", "Massive splenomegaly", "Severe thrombocytopenia with petechiae", "Acute visual deterioration (retinal hemorrhages/cotton-wool spots)", "Elevated uric acid and LDH (consistent with cell turnover/tumor burden)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.8866995073891626, "posterior": 0.5290278254895224, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Leukostasis with fundoscopic findings (retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots) is highly specific to blast crisis in myeloid neoplasms (B1), which supports this branch and undermines chronic/accelerated phase CML (B2) due to the acute presentation.", "The lack of prior chronic MPN symptoms combined with retinal leukostasis is more congruent with de novo myeloid neoplasm (B1) than with CML's chronic/accelerated phase progression (B2), given the typically indolent course of early CML."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of chronic phase symptoms before this acute presentation?", "Recent signs of infection or autoimmune process?", "Known Philadelphia chromosome status?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["BCR-ABL1 transcript testing", "Cytogenetic banding analysis", "Bone marrow aspiration with blast morphology"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.07037297677691766, "posterior": 0.01717622810030917, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["No direct contradiction to myeloid neoplasm was identified despite the high blast count (82%) and retinal signs of leukostasis. These findings align with both de novo AML (B1) and CML in blast crisis (sub-category of B1)."], "evidence_against": ["Leukostasis with fundoscopic findings (retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots) is highly specific to blast crisis in myeloid neoplasms (B1), which supports this branch and undermines chronic/accelerated phase CML (B2) due to the acute presentation.", "The lack of prior chronic MPN symptoms combined with retinal leukostasis is more congruent with de novo myeloid neoplasm (B1) than with CML's chronic/accelerated phase progression (B2), given the typically indolent course of early CML.", "The 82% blasts with acute visual symptoms strongly favor de novo AML (B1.1) as the blast percentage is typical for AML. Retinal leukostasis argues against chronic CML progression (B2) due to the abrupt presentation.", "The 3-week timeline with acute visual symptoms is inconsistent with CML-BC's phase transformation (B1.2) which typically follows a more gradual chronic MPN course. Supports B1.1 as more likely.", "The 3-week subacute trajectory contradicts chronic MPN progression (B2), which typically requires years for transformation. This decisively excludes B2 as a viable explanation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Has the patient had a prior diagnosis of chronic MPN?", "Any family history of myeloid disorders?", "History of polycythemia or thrombosis events?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Ph chromosome/BCR-ABL1 testing", "JAK2 mutation analysis", "Bone marrow fibrosis assessment"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "time_course"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "prior": 0.02814919071076707, "posterior": 0.013740982480247339, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Leukostasis with fundoscopic findings (retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots) is highly specific to blast crisis in myeloid neoplasms (B1), which supports this branch and undermines chronic/accelerated phase CML (B2) due to the acute presentation.", "The lack of prior chronic MPN symptoms combined with retinal leukostasis is more congruent with de novo myeloid neoplasm (B1) than with CML's chronic/accelerated phase progression (B2), given the typically indolent course of early CML."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Any history of lymphadenopathy or autoimmune disease?", "Have blasts shown lymphoid lineage markers on flow cytometry?", "Any signs of central nervous system involvement?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Flow cytometry CD markers (CD10, CD19, TdT)", "Cytogenetic analysis for t(9;22) or other ALL-associated translocations", "Lactate dehydrogenase level"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "prior": 0.011259676284306826, "posterior": 0.005496392992098934, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The lack of prior chronic MPN symptoms combined with retinal leukostasis is more congruent with de novo myeloid neoplasm (B1) than with CML's chronic/accelerated phase progression (B2), given the typically indolent course of early CML."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Any history of monoclonal gammopathy detected in previous labs?", "Has the patient experienced B-cell lymphocytosis in past blood work?", "Have any atypical lymphocytosis patterns been documented?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Immunoglobulin levels and serum protein electrophoresis", "Monoclonal antibody work for lymphoid lineage markers (CD5, CD19, CD20)", "Bone marrow plasma cell assessment"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "pathophysiology"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "prior": 0.003518648838845883, "posterior": 0.001717622810030917, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Leukostasis with fundoscopic findings (retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots) is highly specific to blast crisis in myeloid neoplasms (B1), which supports this branch and undermines chronic/accelerated phase CML (B2) due to the acute presentation.", "The lack of prior chronic MPN symptoms combined with retinal leukostasis is more congruent with de novo myeloid neoplasm (B1) than with CML's chronic/accelerated phase progression (B2), given the typically indolent course of early CML."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the patient have evidence of active infection?", "Have blasts shown clear reactive morphology (e.g., toxic granulation)?", "Any history of chronic inflammation or autoimmune conditions?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Lyme serology and blood cultures", "Coombs test for hemolytic anemia", "Vitamin B12/folate level assessment"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.15, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "pathogenesis"}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4926108374384237, "posterior": 0.4328409481277911, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The 82% blasts with acute visual symptoms strongly favor de novo AML (B1.1) as the blast percentage is typical for AML. Retinal leukostasis argues against chronic CML progression (B2) due to the abrupt presentation.", "The 3-week timeline with acute visual symptoms is inconsistent with CML-BC's phase transformation (B1.2) which typically follows a more gradual chronic MPN course. Supports B1.1 as more likely.", "The 3-week timeline is inconsistent with MDS-EB's (B1.3) gradual blast accumulation. The rapid onset favors de novo AML (B1.1) as MDS-EB rarely presents with sudden 82% blasts."], "evidence_against": ["8% basophilia provides weak support for CML lineage (B1.2) but doesn't outweigh evidence for de novo AML (B1.1) in the absence of prior CML documentation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Absent prior myeloid clonal disorder", "No evidence of myelodysplasia in bone marrow"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Karyotype with absence of Philadelphia chromosome", "Mutation analysis for NPM1, DNMT3A (AML-associated)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis (Phase Transition from Chronic/MPN)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "prior": 0.1970443349753695, "posterior": 0.048093438680865686, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["8% basophilia provides weak support for CML lineage (B1.2) but doesn't outweigh evidence for de novo AML (B1.1) in the absence of prior CML documentation."], "evidence_against": ["The 82% blasts with acute visual symptoms strongly favor de novo AML (B1.1) as the blast percentage is typical for AML. Retinal leukostasis argues against chronic CML progression (B2) due to the abrupt presentation.", "The 3-week timeline with acute visual symptoms is inconsistent with CML-BC's phase transformation (B1.2) which typically follows a more gradual chronic MPN course. Supports B1.1 as more likely.", "The complete absence of prior MPN symptoms decisively undermines B1.2. CML blast crisis requires documented phase progression from earlier CML, not de novo presentation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of chronic phase CML or MPN symptoms prior to this crisis?", "Is there evidence of recent Ph chromosome testing?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Ph chromosome detection via FISH/karyotype", "BCR-ABL1 mutation testing"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "time_course"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB) / Secondary AML", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "prior": 0.1970443349753695, "posterior": 0.048093438680865686, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["82% blasts with splenomegaly are more consistent with acute transformation patterns of myeloid disorders (B1 family) than gradual MDS-EB (B1.3) based on cellularity and timeline."], "evidence_against": ["The 3-week timeline is inconsistent with MDS-EB's (B1.3) gradual blast accumulation. The rapid onset favors de novo AML (B1.1) as MDS-EB rarely presents with sudden 82% blasts."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior myelodysplasia or myelosuppressive therapy?", "Progressive cytopenias over time? (B1.3 is more indolent than B1.1/B1.2)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow cytogenetics (e.g., 5q deletion, complex karyotype)", "Flow cytometry for aberrant lineage expression"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "sub_disease", "classification_axis": "progression"}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.1", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "candidate_leaves": [{"leaf_id": "B1.1::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::0", "branch_id": "B1.1", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 82% blasts in peripheral blood and acute-onset visual symptoms (retinal hemorrhages/cotton-wool spots) more strongly support de novo AML (B1.1) than CML in blast crisis (B1.2) given the lack of prior MPN features?", "expected_information_gain": 0.3, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.1, "action_separation_value": 0.05, "total_score": 0.45, "target_branches": {"B1.1": "support", "B1.2": "against"}, "primary_function": "confirm", "falsification_value": 0.25, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "High blast count with acute leukostasis aligns more with de novo myeloid leukemia than CML transformation."}, {"leaf_id": "B1.1::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::1", "branch_id": "B1.1", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the 8% basophilia argue against de novo AML (B1.1) in favor of CML with accelerated phase transformation (B1.2) as a potential source of blasts?", "expected_information_gain": 0.18, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.05, "action_separation_value": 0.02, "total_score": 0.25, "target_branches": {"B1.1": "against", "B1.2": "support"}, "primary_function": "challenge", "falsification_value": 0.18, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "Basophilia is a feature of CML but not typical for de novo AML."}, {"leaf_id": "B1.2::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::2", "branch_id": "B1.2", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute 3-week clinical trajectory with acute visual deterioration represent CML in blast crisis (B1.2) rather than de novo AML (B1.1)?", "expected_information_gain": 0.25, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.1, "action_separation_value": 0.05, "total_score": 0.4, "target_branches": {"B1.2": "support", "B1.1": "against"}, "primary_function": "confirm", "falsification_value": 0.2, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "Retinal leukostasis in CML-BC is rare but more temporally consistent with transformation pattern"}, {"leaf_id": "B1.2::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::3", "branch_id": "B1.2", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence contradicts CML in blast crisis (B1.2)? Is the absence of documented prior MPN symptoms sufficient to argue against phase transition from chronic CML?", "expected_information_gain": 0.2, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.08, "action_separation_value": 0.05, "total_score": 0.35, "target_branches": {"B1.2": "against", "B1.1": "support"}, "primary_function": "challenge", "falsification_value": 0.17, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "Classic CML with phase transition requires antecedent chronic MPN phase which is absent."}, {"leaf_id": "B1.3::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::4", "branch_id": "B1.3", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute 3-week timeline with 82% blasts in peripheral blood align with MDS-EB's typical gradual progression pattern or does it favor de novo AML (B1.1) with sudden blast predominance?", "expected_information_gain": 0.22, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.1, "action_separation_value": 0.04, "total_score": 0.38, "target_branches": {"B1.3": "against", "B1.1": "support"}, "primary_function": "challenge", "falsification_value": 0.22, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "MDS-EB usually progresses more indolently while abrupt myeloid blast dominance suggests AML."}, {"leaf_id": "B1.3::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::5", "branch_id": "B1.3", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of blasts (82%) and marrow fibrosis (implied by splenomegaly) strongly support myeloid dysplasia/secondary AML (B1.3) as opposed to clonal evolution from prior CMML?", "expected_information_gain": 0.3, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.12, "action_separation_value": 0.06, "total_score": 0.42, "target_branches": {"B1.3": "support"}, "primary_function": "confirm", "falsification_value": 0.0, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "Blast percentage and splenomegaly are consistent with myeloproliferative dysplasia progression."}, {"leaf_id": "B2::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::6", "branch_id": "B2", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "No contradicting evidence identified for Chronic MPN (B2); retinal leukostasis and subacute severe cytopenias align with blast crisis phase.", "expected_information_gain": 0.0, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.0, "action_separation_value": 0.0, "total_score": 0.0, "target_branches": {"B2": "support"}, "primary_function": "confirm", "falsification_value": 0.0, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "All available findings are consistent with the blast crisis presentation pattern."}, {"leaf_id": "B2::ANALYZE_VIGNETTE::7", "branch_id": "B2", "leaf_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence contradicts the Chronic MPN timeline (B2)? Is the 3-week duration inconsistent with chronic/accelerated phase development?", "expected_information_gain": 0.2, "expected_cost": 0.0, "expected_delay": 0.0, "safety_value": 0.08, "action_separation_value": 0.0, "total_score": 0.3, "target_branches": {"B2": "against", "B1.2": "support"}, "primary_function": "challenge", "falsification_value": 0.2, "invasiveness": 0.0, "urgency": "routine", "redundancy_group": "", "bundle_independence": 1.0, "result_dependency": false, "why": "CML typically progresses over years before blast crisis, not suddenly."}], "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 3, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots indicate leukostasis syndrome, which is strongly suggestive of accelerated-phase or blast crisis myeloid neoplasm (B1) over a de novo acute phase presentation (B2)?", "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Do the bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots indicate leukostasis syndrome, which is strongly suggestive of accelerated-phase or blast crisis myeloid neoplasm (B1) over a de novo acute phase presentation (B2)?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "What is the most likely diagnosis?"}, "result_summary": "Leukostasis with fundoscopic findings (retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots) is highly specific to blast crisis in myeloid neoplasms (B1), which supports this branch and undermines chronic/accelerated phase CML (B2) due to the acute presentation.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "strong_for", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "weak_against", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "weak_against"}, "branch_coverage": {"B1": {"confirm_status": "covered", "challenge_status": "covered", "confirm_content": "Do the bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots indicate leukostasis syndrome, which is strongly suggestive of accelerated-phase or blast crisis myeloid neoplasm (B1) over a de novo acute phase presentation (B2)?", "challenge_content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased 